      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I remain unconvinced that RenderType is a common cause of avatars not working with DepthNormals. So far as I could tell, with every shader that I've been able to inspect that isn't working correctly, the RenderType is set such that the replacement shader should be working correctly, but there's some shenanigans (corruption?) happening with the shader/pipeline state.\n\nI've described some of these shenanigans in this canny post:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/the-depthnormals-prepass-appears-to-be-using-incorrect-shader-state-when-shaderl",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
